  "content": [
    {
      "id": "introduction",
      "title": "Introduction",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "You have a collection of elements. You need the&nbsp;<strong>K largest</strong>,&nbsp;<strong>K smallest</strong>, or&nbsp;<strong>K most frequent</strong>&nbsp;not all of them sorted, just the top K.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "The Naive Approach",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Sort everything, take the first K.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Array:&nbsp;<code>[3, 1, 5, 2, 4]</code>, K = 2",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Sort →&nbsp;<code>[1, 2, 3, 4, 5]</code><br>Take last K elements →&nbsp;<code>[4, 5]</code>&nbsp;→ K largest&nbsp;",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Works, but sorting costs&nbsp;<strong>O(n log n)</strong>&nbsp;even when you only care about K elements.",
          "items": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1-the-heap-approach",
      "title": "1. The Heap Approach",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Maintain a heap of&nbsp;<strong>exactly size K</strong>&nbsp;as you scan through the array. At the end, the heap contains exactly the top K elements.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading3",
          "text": "K Largest Elements Use a Min Heap of Size K",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This seems counterintuitive. Why min heap for largest?",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A min heap of size K works like a&nbsp;<strong>filter for top K elements</strong>. The smallest among these K stays at the top, so it’s easy to compare with new elements.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "When a new element comes, if it’s larger than the top, it deserves a place → remove the smallest and insert the new one. After processing all elements, the heap contains the&nbsp;<strong>K largest elements</strong>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "Step by Step (Simple)",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Array:&nbsp;<code>[3, 1, 5, 2, 4]</code>, K = 2",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Process 3 → push → Heap:&nbsp;<code>[3]</code><br><img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406460852-646067058.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Process 1 → push → Heap:&nbsp;<code>[1, 3]</code>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406460853-757962880.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Process 5 → 5 &gt; 1 → remove 1, add 5 → Heap:&nbsp;</span><code style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">[3, 5]</code><br>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406460853-13858246.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Process 2 → 2 &lt; 3 → skip → Heap:&nbsp;</span><code style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">[3, 5]</code><br>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406460853-749113619.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Process 4 → 4 &gt; 3 → remove 3, add 4 → Heap:&nbsp;</span><code style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">[4, 5]</code><br>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "items": [],
          "url": "/engineering/dsa-media/1785406460854-459238981.png",
          "caption": "",
          "content": "/engineering/dsa-media/1785406460854-459238981.png",
          "text": "/engineering/dsa-media/1785406460854-459238981.png",
          "alt": "Step by Step Simple"
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Final heap:&nbsp;<code>[4, 5]</code>&nbsp;→ K largest elements&nbsp;",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "items": [],
          "url": "/engineering/dsa-media/1785406460854-815580976.png",
          "caption": "",
          "content": "/engineering/dsa-media/1785406460854-815580976.png",
          "text": "/engineering/dsa-media/1785406460854-815580976.png",
          "alt": "Step by Step Simple"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "We are keeping track of the&nbsp;<strong>top K largest elements</strong>&nbsp;using a small min heap.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Whenever a new number comes, we check if it is bigger than the smallest in our heap. If yes, we remove the smallest and add the new number; otherwise, we ignore it. At the end, the heap contains the&nbsp;<strong>K largest elements</strong>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "items": [],
          "codes": {
            "javascript": "public int[] kLargest(int[] arr, int k) {\n    PriorityQueue<Integer> minHeap = new PriorityQueue<>();\n\n    for (int num : arr) {\n        minHeap.offer(num);\n\n        if (minHeap.size() > k) {\n            minHeap.poll();    // remove smallest — it doesn't make top K\n        }\n    }\n\n    // heap contains exactly K largest\n    return minHeap.stream().mapToInt(i -> i).toArray();\n}"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Time:&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">O(n log K)</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">&nbsp;for each element, heap operations take log K</span><br>",
            "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Space:&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">O(K)</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">&nbsp;heap size is limited to K</span><br>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "K Smallest Elements Use a Max Heap of Size K",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Exact mirror of K largest. Use a&nbsp;<strong>max heap of size K</strong>&nbsp;if a new element is smaller than the top, it deserves a spot.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Array:&nbsp;<code>[3, 1, 5, 2, 4]</code>, K = 2<br>Find K = 2 smallest",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Process 3 → push → Heap:&nbsp;<code>[3]</code><br><img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406460854-747211588.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Process 1 → push → Heap:&nbsp;</span><code style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">[3, 1]</code><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">&nbsp;(top = 3)</span><br>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406460855-847245302.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Process 5 → 5 &gt; 3 → skip</span><br>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406460855-708175161.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Process 2 → 2 &lt; 3 → remove 3, add 2 → Heap:&nbsp;</span><code style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">[2, 1]</code><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">&nbsp;(top = 2)</span><br>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406461040-965081883.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\"><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Process 4 → 4 &gt; 2 → skip</span>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406461041-773922028.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Result:&nbsp;</span><code style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">[1, 2]</code><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">&nbsp;✓&nbsp;</span><br>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "items": [],
          "url": "/engineering/dsa-media/1785406461041-156339419.png",
          "caption": "",
          "content": "/engineering/dsa-media/1785406461041-156339419.png",
          "text": "/engineering/dsa-media/1785406461041-156339419.png",
          "alt": "K Smallest Elements Use a Max Heap of Size K"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "We are keeping track of the&nbsp;<strong>K smallest elements</strong>&nbsp;using a max heap.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The heap stores K elements, and the largest among them stays at the top. When a new number comes, if it is smaller than the top, we remove the largest and add the new number; otherwise, we ignore it. In the end, the heap contains the&nbsp;<strong>K smallest elements</strong>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "items": [],
          "codes": {
            "javascript": "public int[] kSmallest(int[] arr, int k) {\n    PriorityQueue<Integer> maxHeap = new PriorityQueue<>(Collections.reverseOrder());\n\n    for (int num : arr) {\n        maxHeap.offer(num);\n\n        if (maxHeap.size() > k) {\n            maxHeap.poll();    // remove largest — it doesn't make bottom K\n        }\n    }\n\n    return maxHeap.stream().mapToInt(i -> i).toArray();\n}"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "2-the-mental-model",
      "title": "2. The Mental Model",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "K largest → use&nbsp;<strong>min heap of size K</strong><br>(min heap removes smallest → keeps largest elements)",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "K smallest → use&nbsp;<strong>max heap of size K</strong><br>(max heap removes largest → keeps smallest elements)",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<b>Rule</b>:<br>heap type = opposite of what you want<br>heap size = exactly K<br>if size &gt; K → remove top<br>end → heap contains the answer&nbsp;",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This is a&nbsp;<strong>simple rule to decide which heap to use</strong>&nbsp;when finding top K elements.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "When you want&nbsp;<strong>K largest</strong>, you use a&nbsp;<strong>min heap</strong>&nbsp;so that the smallest among those K stays at the top. If a bigger element comes, the small one gets removed, and only large elements remain.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "When you want&nbsp;<strong>K smallest</strong>, you use a&nbsp;<strong>max heap</strong>&nbsp;so that the largest among those K stays at the top. If a smaller element comes, the large one gets removed, and only small elements remain.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "text": "So the idea is: use the&nbsp;<strong>opposite heap</strong>&nbsp;to filter out unwanted elements and keep only the K you need&nbsp;",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        }
      ]
    }
